WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250
I am aware that I inhale, I am aware that I exhale,

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.780
I am my breath, I become aware of my body,

3
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.074
I relax my body, I generate

4
00:00:10.104 --> 00:00:13.174
a feeling of joy, I generate a feeling of happiness

5
00:00:13.204 --> 00:00:14.470
in the present.

6
00:00:17.493 --> 00:00:20.877
I become aware of my pain, I embrace my pain,

7
00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:22.133
I take care of it.

8
00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:25.917
It is important to have good motivation when you

9
00:00:25.947 --> 00:00:27.022
start to meditate.

10
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.067
will present you with obstacles.

11
00:00:30.097 --> 00:00:33.257
The first obstacle you will encounter is laziness.

12
00:00:33.287 --> 00:00:35.697
It will bring you a second subtlety,

13
00:00:35.727 --> 00:00:37.577
which is called active laziness.

14
00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:38.617
I was doing a

15
00:00:39.466 --> 00:00:42.161
lot of things except going to meditate.

16
00:00:42.191 --> 00:00:45.174
A third form of laziness that still arises is

17
00:00:45.204 --> 00:00:46.309
abandonment.

18
00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:49.932
But then you tell yourself no, ultimately it's not

19
00:00:49.962 --> 00:00:50.518
for me.

20
00:00:50.548 --> 00:00:51.190
The antidote

21
00:00:52.111 --> 00:00:53.631
is to find a proper motivation.

22
00:00:54.848 --> 00:00:57.228
This motivation must be not only for yourself,

23
00:00:57.258 --> 00:00:58.348
but also for others.

24
00:00:59.006 --> 00:01:01.673
The second real obstacle you will encounter,

25
00:01:02.335 --> 00:01:04.197
is that when you learn to meditate,

26
00:01:04.227 --> 00:01:06.828
initially, there is a methodology in learning.

27
00:01:07.127 --> 00:01:09.238
The obstacle you will encounter is the complete

28
00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:10.740
forgetting of what needs to be done.

29
00:01:11.698 --> 00:01:13.436
At one point, I was meditating, or rather,

30
00:01:13.466 --> 00:01:14.978
I thought I was meditating,

31
00:01:15.395 --> 00:01:17.035
I was sitting there, ultimately,

32
00:01:17.065 --> 00:01:18.287
I was quite lost in thought.

33
00:01:19.016 --> 00:01:21.166
I understood that meditation is a training of the

34
00:01:21.196 --> 00:01:21.586
mind.

35
00:01:21.811 --> 00:01:23.839
It comes from a very ancient etymology which

36
00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:24.401
means...

37
00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.317
Truly learning to discover one's own functioning.

38
00:01:28.024 --> 00:01:29.606
You are not always well when you meditate,

39
00:01:29.636 --> 00:01:30.284
but that's okay.

40
00:01:30.404 --> 00:01:33.014
I learn to recognize, to train my mind.

41
00:01:33.203 --> 00:01:35.990
And the antidote, which I think is very interesting

42
00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.589
for us in the practice of meditation,

43
00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:39.293
is attention, is mindfulness.

44
00:01:39.703 --> 00:01:41.821
To discover this energy that is in your mind,

45
00:01:41.851 --> 00:01:43.603
this energy which is concentration,

46
00:01:43.983 --> 00:01:46.034
and which will gradually open you to another energy,

47
00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:47.578
which is the profound vision of things.

48
00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:48.953
But one must proceed gradually.

49
00:01:49.495 --> 00:01:52.303
It's like when you enter a space where on the walls.

50
00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:54.305
There are secrets that can be unveiled.

51
00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:56.847
I enter with a candle, and the candle is your mind.

52
00:01:57.171 --> 00:01:59.549
Initially, the candle flickers like this,

53
00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:01.571
meaning there isn't much luminosity.

54
00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:04.824
But if, through the foundational practice of your

55
00:02:04.854 --> 00:02:07.724
meditation, you learn to completely stabilize the

56
00:02:07.754 --> 00:02:10.154
flame, a kind of luminous halo appears,

57
00:02:10.184 --> 00:02:11.674
a clarity that emerges.

58
00:02:13.063 --> 00:02:15.018
Well, it's somewhat the same thing.

59
00:02:15.048 --> 00:02:17.476
If you truly manage to stabilize your mind,

60
00:02:17.506 --> 00:02:19.945
suddenly you will perceive a kind of luminous

61
00:02:19.975 --> 00:02:20.567
clarity.

62
00:02:20.597 --> 00:02:22.367
that appears in one's mind.

63
00:02:22.397 --> 00:02:25.506
This clarity leads you to profound insight.

64
00:02:25.972 --> 00:02:28.558
One must learn to stabilize the mind because it is

65
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:30.465
an entire process of stabilization.

66
00:02:30.495 --> 00:02:31.932
Therefore, it is learning

67
00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.770
to develop this clarity of mind primarily through

68
00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.328
the energy of mindfulness,

69
00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.438
concentration, and the energy of profound insight.

70
00:02:43.602 --> 00:02:47.150
One must practice. Everyone can access this.

